.TH TAIL 1
.SH NAME
tail \- deliver the last part of a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tail
[
.BI + number
|
.BI \- number
|
.B \-n
.I number
]
[
.I file
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Tail
copies the named file to the standard output beginning
at a designated line.
If no file is named, the standard input is copied.
.PP
Copying begins at line
.BI + number
measured from the beginning, or
.I number
lines from the end of the input under
.BI \- number
or
.B \-n
.IR number .
The default is the last 10 lines.
Lines from the beginning count from 1.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B tail file
Print the last 10 lines of a file.
.TP
.B tail +2 file
Print a file from its second line on.
.TP
.B sed 10q file
Print the first 10 lines of a file.
.SH SOURCE
.B cmd/tail/main.odin
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR sed (1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The exit status is empty,
.B "can't open"
when the file could not be opened, or
.B "read error"
when it could not be read.
.SH BUGS
The whole input is read into memory before anything is printed.
There is no
.B \-f
and no
.BR \-c .
.I Tail
counts lines only.
